1
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:42,840
Somehow we'll manage, right?

2
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without work, come to me.

3
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

4
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:11,560
Look, even the steel is burning.

5
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:18,260
Somehow, eventually, we'll make it work.

6
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:23,540
You understand, right?
I understand, I understand.

7
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,380
Once you get it, keep quiet and follow me.

8
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:39,860
Mm.

9
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:44,060
Chief Ohara gets hooked on games.

10
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:44,920
Mm.

11
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:49,420
Well, is that so

12
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:52,060
What are you doing?

13
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:59,880
Yeah, all right! Kah! Kyaa! Kyaho-ran!

14
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:05,220
Wow, you seem to be
having a lot of fun, Ryo-2.

15
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:07,260
Well, of course I am.

16
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:10,260
For the past week, I've been sneaking
around behind the Chief's back

17
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:13,820
playing and playing and playing nonstop,
and I've finally cleared it.

18
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:16,420
I see, I see.

19
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:21,260
Yeah, the trouble I went
through to keep it from the Chief!

20
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:28,540
You idiot!

21
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:29,660
Bah, Chief!

22
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:32,880
Come on, Chief.

23
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:35,100
When did you get here?

24
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:37,800
If you were here,
you should've said so sooner!

25
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:39,880
You really are something else.

26
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:43,380
The moment I look away,
you slack off on your work.

27
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:47,160
You've been playing games
nonstop for a whole week?

28
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:49,820
Well in between my work,

29
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:53,080
I only started it as a little break,
that's all.

30
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:57,360
Without even realizing it,
I just kept on playing and playing.

31
00:02:57,360 --> 00:03:01,540
Well, games are a terrifying thing, Chief.

32
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:04,760
Once you get hooked, you just can't stop.

33
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:07,620
Why don't you give it a try too, Chief?

34
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:09,240
You idiot!

35
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:12,180
As if I'd ever play a game!

36
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:15,380
What do you think work is supposed to be?

37
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:17,420
A break between tasks?

38
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:21,820
You take breaks nonstop
and never do any work at all!

39
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:24,780
I'm confiscating this.

40
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:27,500
No way! Give it back!

41
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:29,740
Quiet! No arguments!

42
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:32,740
From now on,
don't you dare bring games into the station!

43
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:33,820
Understood?

44
00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:34,220
Yes!

45
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:38,080
This too.

46
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:45,940
These too.

47
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:51,600
This one too.

48
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:53,540
I'll dispose of all of them myself!

49
00:03:54,780 --> 00:03:57,760
I swear I won't play games,
so please give them back.

50
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:00,080
Those are my life.

51
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:02,780
Who would believe such a thing?

52
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:06,480
Honestly, a grown man shouldn't
keep playing games forever!

53
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:09,920
The trouble is, games are so fun
for adults that I can't help it.

54
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:11,960
Idiot!

55
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:14,120
Stop goofing off and...

56
00:04:14,820 --> 00:04:18,680
It's like a tantrum-throwing
schoolkid fighting with his mother.

57
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:19,520
Exactly.

58
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:21,340
Chief, please!

59
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:26,760
Each one of those games is
a treasure box of my memories.

60
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:28,620
Hey, let go!

61
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:34,380
Okay, good kids, everyone!

62
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:36,200
It's a present for everyone!

63
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:38,660
Go grab whichever game you like.

64
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:46,820
Okay, okay, don't push.

65
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:49,820
One at a time, there's plenty for everyone.

66
00:04:51,340 --> 00:04:51,820
That's it for now.

67
00:04:51,820 --> 00:04:52,820
Whoa, this one...

68
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:56,040
Whoa, games, games!

69
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,240
Hey, those are mine!

70
00:04:58,680 --> 00:04:59,860
I said this one's no good either.

71
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,920
Ryotsu,
you and that guy need to give up already.

72
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:06,520
You good-for-nothing.

73
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:08,260
No, Grandpa, stop it.

74
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:10,091
Listen, Ryotsu,

75
00:05:10,141 --> 00:05:13,200
No more games from now on, understand?

76
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:15,280
And don't you dare do it again.

77
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:16,640
Got it?

78
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:17,800
Y-yes, sir.

79
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:19,740
Grandpa!

80
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:23,460
Daisuke, you came?

81
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:26,700
Yeah, with Mom and Sakura.

82
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,700
I see, I see.
Well, I'm glad you came, Daisuke.

83
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:31,700
Grandpa, this is for you.

84
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:33,580
What's this?

85
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:36,000
It's a present for Grandpa.

86
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:42,260
I see, it's a present for Grandpa.

87
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:44,580
Thank you, Daisuke. Thank you.

88
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,360
Now, what could Daisuke's present be?

89
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:50,580
W-what's this?

90
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:52,520
A shogi game?

91
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:56,542
Yeah! Grandpa always
plays shogi alone at home,

92
00:05:56,592 --> 00:05:58,480
so with this, you won't have to
worry about finding an opponent, right?

93
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:00,866
When we went to the
department store the other day,

94
00:06:00,916 --> 00:06:04,820
Daisuke insisted he had to buy it for Grandpa,
wouldn't take no for an answer.

95
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:07,120
That's wonderful, dear.

96
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:08,280
Y-yes.

97
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:10,720
Hey, try it, try it!

98
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:11,840
Yes, let's do that.

99
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:15,875
B-but, having just said all that to Ryotsu,

100
00:06:15,925 --> 00:06:17,780
I can't very well accept this myself.

101
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:20,600
Come on, Grandpa.

102
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,840
Let's try it already, hurry up!

103
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:27,960
If there's anything you don't understand,
I'll teach you.

104
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:29,100
S-so I see.

105
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:35,160
Wow.

106
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:38,360
Even though it's so small,
it's a proper shogi board.

107
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:41,420
You move the cursor with this cross key.

108
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:42,580
Cursor?

109
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:44,360
This arrow here.

110
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:47,620
Then, once you select the piece you want to move,
press the B button.

111
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:49,620
B button.

112
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:51,940
It moved.

113
00:06:51,940 --> 00:06:53,580
The opponent's pieces too.

114
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,020
This is amazing.

115
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:05,400
Dear.

116
00:07:06,140 --> 00:07:08,440
Were you playing shogi?

117
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,760
Be quiet.

118
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:11,340
This is an important part right now.

119
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:12,340
Don't talk to me.

120
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:30,520
Good, Master, you're calling a take-back!

121
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:32,220
How about that?

122
00:07:34,060 --> 00:07:35,480
So you're going with this move?

123
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,640
As expected of a master.

124
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:41,360
If I go, you come, then I go...

125
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:42,820
This pawn...

126
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:50,800
I was so absorbed in the game,
I didn't notice.

127
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,440
Close, close!

128
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,240
He's agonizing again.

129
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:59,260
But there's no escape for you now!

130
00:08:00,260 --> 00:08:01,640
So that's how you're playing.

131
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:03,920
I see, then I'll move my rook...

132
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,740
No, here, the knight...

133
00:08:06,740 --> 00:08:09,200
No, no, then I won't be able to move.

134
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:11,120
Here, after all...

135
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:11,480
Chief.

136
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:14,600
I've finished compiling the daily report.

137
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:15,880
I see.

138
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:22,760
You startled me.

139
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:25,840
Don't be so surprised when someone
suddenly calls out from behind you.

140
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:28,820
especially when you
have a guilty conscience.

141
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:31,380
I'm starting to understand how Ryotsu feels.

142
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:34,140
At this rate,
I'll end up on the same level as him.

143
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:37,620
Let's stop with the games.

144
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:39,440
Work, work.

145
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:42,380
Same day, 6:03.

146
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:43,620
Kameari Park.

147
00:08:43,620 --> 00:08:46,360
6:03.

148
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,620
I hadn't thought of that.

149
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:51,940
Pawn to three, how about this?

150
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,400
Counter-check!

151
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,300
What should I do?

152
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:02,480
This won't do, this won't do.

153
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:05,440
This is exactly like Ryotsu!

154
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:07,360
I'll forget about the games now.

155
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:09,060
Right now, it's work.

156
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:12,360
At Kameari Park.

157
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,340
That's right, the bishop!

158
00:09:21,340 --> 00:09:23,140
Bishop to 3-4.

159
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:26,480
And when the opponent tries to run away,

160
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:29,520
gold to 5-4,

161
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:32,240
if I press the attack,
there's no escape route.

162
00:09:33,020 --> 00:09:34,060
That's it!

163
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:37,700
This won't do, this won't do.

164
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:40,160
I can't seem to stop playing games.

165
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:41,780
I have to forget about it.

166
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:43,860
Time to work, work!

167
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:04,920
Mm...

168
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:06,380
Mm...

169
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:09,100
Mm...

170
00:10:09,180 --> 00:10:10,040
Mm...

171
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:23,240
One more move.

172
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,380
Just one more move.

173
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:25,800
This'll be the last one.

174
00:10:28,580 --> 00:10:30,800
Well, since this goes here like this...

175
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,580
So here, it goes like this.

176
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:34,080
I see, I see.

177
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:36,600
I did it!

178
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,740
I finally beat the master!

179
00:10:38,740 --> 00:10:41,120
What's wrong, Chief?

180
00:10:42,180 --> 00:10:43,780
Nothing, never mind.

181
00:10:47,780 --> 00:10:48,940
That was close, that was close.

182
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:52,300
I'd decided I would only talk about it,
but I got absorbed in it.

183
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:55,480
If Ryotsu caught me in a place like this,
it would be a disaster.

184
00:10:59,060 --> 00:11:00,800
What's wrong with you, anyway?

185
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:04,020
Ryotsu, you'd be startled, wouldn't you?

186
00:11:04,020 --> 00:11:06,660
Is there anyone who just suddenly
speaks to someone like that?

187
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:10,560
Then what am I supposed to do
when I have business with you?

188
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:13,860
So should I just stay silent?

189
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,820
Am I not allowed to say
anything to the Chief at all?

190
00:11:18,020 --> 00:11:18,640
Shut up!

191
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,900
Don't talk back to me every single time!

192
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:22,660
Get out of here and go over there, now!

193
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:23,381
Mutter, mutter.

194
00:11:23,431 --> 00:11:26,820
But this time it's not my fault at all,
mutter, mutter.

195
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:28,060
I said go already, just go!

196
00:11:28,160 --> 00:11:28,500
Yes, sir.

197
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:31,740
What's with the Chief today, honestly.

198
00:11:32,060 --> 00:11:34,380
The Chief seems a bit strange, doesn't he?

199
00:11:34,660 --> 00:11:37,160
He's been unusually restless since earlier.

200
00:11:42,180 --> 00:11:43,560
Nnngh...

201
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:45,120
Phew...

202
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:56,340
There's definitely something going on.

203
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:59,060
Something I can't tell them...

204
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:06,680
Let's see, here...

205
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:07,560
Here, it's like this, Kei-chan.

206
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,300
No, here it's like that, Nakagawa.

207
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:14,820
This is bad. I'm being suspected.
I can't play games here anymore.

208
00:12:20,060 --> 00:12:21,840
I'm going on patrol.

209
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:34,400
Just this one game, just this one.

210
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:36,880
Chief.

211
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:42,060
What is it, Ryotsu? What's wrong?

212
00:12:42,060 --> 00:12:46,000
I thought I'd go on
patrol with the Chief too.

213
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,900
No, you don't have to tag along.

214
00:12:48,900 --> 00:12:51,760
You go back to the police
box and get to work.

215
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:54,520
Don't be so stiff about it, come on.

216
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:56,540
Come on, come on, let's go, let's go.

217
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:05,740
What lovely weather, Chief.

218
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:08,760
The town's peaceful, too.
Nothing to complain about.

219
00:13:09,220 --> 00:13:10,020
Yeah.

220
00:13:12,780 --> 00:13:15,220
Hey, Ryotsu,
how far are you planning to follow me?

221
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:17,880
I'll accompany you wherever you go.

222
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:21,080
After all, you're my respected superior.

223
00:13:22,300 --> 00:13:23,420
Damn it.

224
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:26,180
That Ryotsu, using this as an excuse...

225
00:13:26,540 --> 00:13:30,540
Hold on... let me make my next move.
Hurry up and let me play!

226
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:39,100
Yeah, just as I thought.

227
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:40,060
Chief.

228
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:41,380
Whoa!

229
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:43,060
What are you doing?

230
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:45,480
Sorry, sorry.

231
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:49,600
That girl is cute, isn't she? I wonder what class she's in.
I think it's Fifth Year, Class Three.

232
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:52,820
Fifth year, class three, five-three, four.

233
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:55,000
So that's the trick.

234
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:59,380
...was. No, nothing, nothing at all!

235
00:14:01,900 --> 00:14:02,900
Nine.

236
00:14:12,420 --> 00:14:13,420
Me.

237
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:47,980
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

238
00:14:47,980 --> 00:14:48,800
Ohhh, no...

239
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:55,920
So that's what it is.

240
00:14:55,920 --> 00:15:00,080
After I had the nerve to
pompously ban games for myself,

241
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:02,140
just watch what I do.

242
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:27,000
Here...

243
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,180
It's like this, see.

244
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:31,940
There are two lost items...

245
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:57,380
Nakagawa, isn't it about
time we headed to the station?

246
00:15:57,380 --> 00:15:58,120
Yes, I suppose so.

247
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:01,300
Reiko, would you go on patrol?

248
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:02,600
Yes, understood.

249
00:16:12,780 --> 00:16:14,340
Chief, is something wrong?

250
00:16:14,340 --> 00:16:16,900
No, nothing.

251
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:21,060
Ugh, of all times,
work has to pile up right now!

252
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:26,980
Chief, I'll go on patrol too.

253
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:29,180
I see.

254
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:46,160
Finally, everyone's gone.

255
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:56,880
Now, the master's match!

256
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:00,400
Here we go, too!

257
00:17:10,340 --> 00:17:13,340
Now beginning the second stage.

258
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:18,100
So you're today's opponent?

259
00:17:18,820 --> 00:17:19,880
It talked.

260
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:24,160
Challenging me, of all people?
How presumptuous!

261
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:25,820
I'll beat you right back.

262
00:17:29,140 --> 00:17:32,540
I see, so this is how
the second stage is set up.

263
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:34,200
Right, I won't lose!

264
00:17:37,440 --> 00:17:40,160
What's wrong, master? Isn't it your turn?

265
00:17:41,840 --> 00:17:45,480
The one who panics loses.
That's the golden rule of this game.

266
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:49,280
Psychological warfare, is it?
As expected of a master.

267
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:54,240
It's lovely weather today, don't you think?

268
00:17:55,120 --> 00:17:55,920
Indeed.

269
00:17:55,920 --> 00:17:59,500
On days like this, you just want
to forget all about work, don't you?

270
00:18:00,220 --> 00:18:01,280
Quite so.

271
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:04,340
A scheme to drain my motivation, is it?

272
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:05,700
I won't fall for that trick.

273
00:18:06,780 --> 00:18:07,180
What?

274
00:18:08,940 --> 00:18:12,040
Master, please leave this small fry to me.

275
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:15,280
What, calling me a small fry?

276
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:17,760
If you beat me, I'll acknowledge you.

277
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:20,300
I'll give you an interesting match.

278
00:18:23,420 --> 00:18:24,600
How about this?

279
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:34,960
Curse you,
you're pulling a cowardly Ryotsu-style move!

280
00:18:35,620 --> 00:18:39,080
Player,
you've used up your allotted thinking time,

281
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:42,700
so from now on,
please make each move within 30 seconds.

282
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:44,200
What?

283
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:47,960
I'm back.

284
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:51,540
What? It suddenly turned
into a speed shogi match!

285
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:52,980
Chief?

286
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:56,880
What is it, Nakagawa?

287
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:58,880
What's wrong, Chief?

288
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:00,140
Well...

289
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:02,060
20 seconds left.

290
00:19:04,340 --> 00:19:06,520
I'm going out on patrol for a bit.

291
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:13,040
Uh, if the gold moves like this...

292
00:19:15,180 --> 00:19:16,460
10 seconds left.

293
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:21,100
8, 7, 6.

294
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:22,800
How about this?

295
00:19:24,020 --> 00:19:24,880
I yield.

296
00:19:25,780 --> 00:19:28,120
With 147 points, that concludes the match.

297
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:30,300
The winner is Mr. Crayer.

298
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:35,260
I lost to you.

299
00:19:35,260 --> 00:19:38,380
Then as a penalty, I'll take my clothes off.

300
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:41,240
Stop it, knock it off!

301
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:43,940
I don't need you to do
something like that...

302
00:19:43,940 --> 00:19:44,160
Come on.

303
00:19:45,620 --> 00:19:48,620
Don't stare at me like that,
it's embarrassing!

304
00:19:48,620 --> 00:19:49,060
Day.

305
00:20:00,580 --> 00:20:01,620
What a disaster!

306
00:20:01,620 --> 00:20:04,800
I never expected such a turn of events.

307
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:06,120
Later.

308
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:09,560
Then I'll be your opponent.

309
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:11,800
So, the master match at last.

310
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:13,520
Bring it on.

311
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:15,400
What?

312
00:20:24,020 --> 00:20:24,600
Aaaaaah!

313
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:33,600
Aaaaaah! If you crash, it's game over! If you
want to face the master, you'd better catch up.

314
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:35,440
Then, ready... go!

315
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:43,680
Why did it switch to a car game?
I've never played a game like this.

316
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:44,140
Aaaaaah!

317
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:48,480
It's the car the master is riding in.

318
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:53,120
Give me back the master!

319
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:56,020
Aaaaaah!

320
00:20:56,020 --> 00:20:57,180
Damn it.

321
00:20:57,180 --> 00:20:58,100
Dammit!

322
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:01,680
Alright, time for the final touch.

323
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:04,880
Whoa! Master!

324
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:15,040
I'll give you credit for that.

325
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:17,080
Finally, it's over

326
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:20,180
Fine, if you want the Meijin back,

327
00:21:20,620 --> 00:21:23,080
you'll have to race me in a marathon!

328
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:24,900
Marathon?

329
00:21:25,420 --> 00:21:28,000
Then you'll run exactly as I tell you.

330
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,540
By the way,
this game has a built-in speedometer.

331
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:35,260
If you fall behind me even a little,
I won't return the Meijin.

332
00:21:35,260 --> 00:21:36,220
What did you say?

333
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:37,360
Then...

334
00:21:37,360 --> 00:21:38,520
Ready...

335
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:41,520
Hey.

336
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:41,980
Hey!

337
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:43,600
Come on, hurry up and run!

338
00:21:45,640 --> 00:21:47,700
Meijin, I'm coming to save you!

339
00:21:57,220 --> 00:21:58,720
Yes, keep going straight!

340
00:22:00,540 --> 00:22:03,000
Why do I have to run?!

341
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:04,260
Okay, turn right there!

342
00:22:07,260 --> 00:22:07,760
Aaaaaaah!

343
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:08,840
Eeeeeeeh!

344
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:10,680
Eeeeeeeh!

345
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:11,260
Eeeeeeeh!

346
00:22:11,260 --> 00:22:11,580
Eeeeeeeh!

347
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,340
Eeeeeeeh!

348
00:22:13,340 --> 00:22:14,000
Eeeeeeeh!

349
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:23,400
Yay!

350
00:22:27,620 --> 00:22:28,480
Okay, jump there!

351
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:37,620
Right there! Left there!
Okay, straight ahead!

352
00:22:38,080 --> 00:22:41,940
Okay, right! Left!
Now diagonal! Okay, straight!

353
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:47,100
Give back the Meijin...

354
00:23:01,080 --> 00:23:02,920
The goal is almost here.

355
00:23:05,360 --> 00:23:07,060
Keep going there!

356
00:23:07,060 --> 00:23:09,200
Goal!

357
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:11,460
Yes!

358
00:23:11,460 --> 00:23:14,620
Big-bellied Kron

359
00:23:18,680 --> 00:23:20,840
Just a little more.

360
00:23:49,420 --> 00:23:50,001
So that's it,

361
00:23:50,051 --> 00:23:54,000
I knew something was off with this game.
It's all Ryotsu's doing!

362
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,360
Damn you, how dare you

363
00:23:55,360 --> 00:23:57,820
Hey! Ryotsu!

364
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:02,060
You were having quite a
good time yourself, Chief!

365
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:14,100
Why is that, why is that?

366
00:24:14,100 --> 00:24:14,820
Why is that?

367
00:24:14,820 --> 00:24:15,500
Why is that?

368
00:24:15,500 --> 00:24:16,280
Why is that?

369
00:24:16,280 --> 00:24:17,380
Ryo-san's...

370
00:24:17,380 --> 00:24:18,280
Why is that?

371
00:24:19,700 --> 00:24:23,880
Ryo-san's eyebrows look like black seagulls.

372
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:24,900
I wonder why.

373
00:24:24,900 --> 00:24:26,200
I wonder why.

374
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:30,340
Even though he wears sandals,
he can run really fast.

375
00:24:30,340 --> 00:24:31,360
I wonder why.

376
00:24:31,360 --> 00:24:33,080
I wonder why.

377
00:24:33,980 --> 00:24:38,220
Ryo-san always has his sleeves rolled up.

378
00:24:38,220 --> 00:24:39,240
I wonder why.

379
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:40,520
I wonder why.

380
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:45,660
He's a total mess, yet everyone looks up to him.
I wonder why.

381
00:24:46,130 --> 00:24:47,780
I wonder why.

382
00:24:48,460 --> 00:24:51,540
It doesn't really matter, but...

383
00:24:52,560 --> 00:24:58,320
Why is this anime's title so long?

384
00:24:58,320 --> 00:25:01,100
Kochira Katsushika-ku
Kameari Kōen-mae Hashutsujo

385
00:25:01,100 --> 00:25:02,920
I wonder why.

386
00:25:02,920 --> 00:25:05,320
I wonder why.

387
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:08,440
I wonder why.

388
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:09,680
I wonder why.

389
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:10,880
Why is that?

390
00:25:10,880 --> 00:25:11,640
Why is that?

391
00:25:11,640 --> 00:25:11,960
Why is that?

392
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:13,700
Why is that?

393
00:25:13,700 --> 00:25:18,820
I wonder why.

394
00:25:30,740 --> 00:25:33,760
What? Lemon has foods he doesn't like?

395
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:37,240
At this rate, he'll be in trouble with school
lunches once he starts elementary school, right?

396
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:38,660
Alright, leave it to me.

397
00:25:38,660 --> 00:25:40,880
I'll cure those likes and dislikes of his.

398
00:25:40,880 --> 00:25:42,940
So, what exactly can't he eat?

399
00:25:43,400 --> 00:25:45,940
Next time: Lemon, the Picky Eating King!

400
00:25:46,300 --> 00:25:46,980
See you then.

401
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:50,820
That's Kameari-ee.

402
00:25:51,880 --> 00:25:54,000
Well, surely at Kameari,

403
00:25:55,140 --> 00:25:59,180
everyone, come on over to our town!

404
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:00,840
Thank you.

